I hold the coffee cup carefully in my hand.
This is my second coffee.
I walk to the counter with pride.
A woman is waiting there for her coffee.
I place the cup in front of her.
"Here is your coffee, didi," I tell her politely.
The woman takes the cup and smiles at me.
"Thank you," she says.
I feel very happy.
I had made the first coffee completely wrong.
But I made this second coffee perfectly.
Sunita is watching all this from near the espresso machine.
"Very nice, Maya," Sunita says to me.
I am now learning to use the coffee machine properly.
Also, I am learning to talk to the customers.
This work is new for me.
But I am liking this experience a lot.
I get ready for the next order with fresh enthusiasm.
